{% extends 'layout.twig' %}
{% import 'partials/macros.twig' as m %}
{% block main %}
    <section class="page-intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">Features</p>
        <h1 id="page-title">Features</h1>
        <p class="lede">What SightPress can do in test release {{ site.release.version }}, and what comes next.</p>
        <div class="callout">
          <h2 class="callout-title">Test releases are for developers and testers</h2>
          <p>You can install SightPress on your own computer and try everything listed under <a href="#now">Available now</a>. It isn’t ready for live websites yet: running it on a public server is covered from version 1.0.</p>
        </div>
        <nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-title">
          <h2 id="toc-title" class="toc-title">On this page</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#now">Available now ({{ site.release.version }})</a></li>
            <li><a href="#in-progress">In progress ({{ site.next.version }})</a></li>
            <li><a href="#before-1-0">Before 1.0</a></li>
            <li><a href="#after-1-0">After 1.0</a></li>
            <li><a href="#try">Try it</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="now" aria-labelledby="now-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">Available in {{ site.release.version }}</p>
        <h2 id="now-title">Available now</h2>
        <p class="lede">Everything in this section works in test release {{ site.release.version }}. Each item links to a step-by-step guide in the documentation.</p>
        <div class="feature-groups">
          <section class="feature-group" aria-labelledby="f-writing">
            <h3 id="f-writing">{{ m.icon('edit') }} Writing and publishing</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
              <li>Build pages from thirteen kinds of block: heading, text, image, gallery, video, audio, file download, columns, call to action, contact form, list of pages, sign language video, and a video or map from another site that loads nothing until the reader asks. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/write-and-publish-a-page/') }}">Write and publish a page</a></li>
              <li>Give each block its own look: a background, a width and the space around it. Every theme’s colours are checked, so text stays readable on every background.</li>
              <li>Pages move from draft through review to published, and can be published or taken down at a set time. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/schedule-a-page/') }}">Schedule a page</a></li>
              <li>Compare any older version word by word, with changes written out as “removed” and “added”, and restore it without publishing it. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/restore-an-older-version/') }}">Restore an older version</a></li>
              <li>Copy, archive, trash and move pages, with redirects that keep old addresses working. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/move-or-rename-a-page/') }}">Move or rename a page</a></li>
              <li>Menus, and an audit log of who changed what.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
          <section class="feature-group" aria-labelledby="f-accessible">
            <h3 id="f-accessible">{{ m.icon('accessibility') }} Accessible by default</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
              <li>An admin panel designed to be used with a keyboard and a screen reader: upload progress is announced, and the menu shows only what your role can use.</li>
              <li>Checks before publishing: image descriptions, link text, captions, transcripts and heading order. An accessibility error stops a page from being published until it is fixed.</li>
              <li>Images need a description, or an explicit choice to mark them as decorative.</li>
              <li>Each new site starts with ready-made pages, including an accessibility statement. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/create-a-site/') }}">Create a website</a></li>
            </ul>
          </section>
          <section class="feature-group" aria-labelledby="f-sites">
            <h3 id="f-sites">{{ m.icon('language') }} Several sites and languages</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
              <li>One installation runs several websites, each with its own people, pages and files.</li>
              <li>Each page can have a translation in any available language, with its own title, address and content. Translations start as drafts. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/add-a-language/') }}">Add a language</a></li>
              <li>Search engines are told which pages are translations of each other, and each language has its own sitemap.</li>
              <li>The admin panel, site texts and emails are in UK English, European Portuguese and Spanish. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/translate-sightpress/') }}">Translate SightPress</a></li>
            </ul>
          </section>
          <section class="feature-group" aria-labelledby="f-people">
            <h3 id="f-people">{{ m.icon('users') }} People and sign-in</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
              <li>Invite people, or let them create their own account. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/let-people-sign-up/') }}">Let people sign up</a></li>
              <li>Make single pages, or a whole site, readable only by signed-in members; those pages stay out of search engines. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/make-a-site-members-only/') }}">Make a site members-only</a></li>
              <li>Password resets, invitations and new accounts use a six-digit code that you type on a page, never a link in an email. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/codes-we-send-you/') }}">Codes we send you</a></li>
              <li>Create your own roles with exactly the permissions someone needs, each explained in plain English. SightPress won’t let you remove the last admin or lock yourself out. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/create-a-custom-role/') }}">Create a custom role</a></li>
              <li>Allow only your organisation’s email addresses to join, and only its domain names for websites. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/keep-websites-to-your-organisation/') }}">Keep websites to your organisation</a></li>
              <li>Optional text messages, off until someone connects a provider and sets a monthly budget: notifications, signing in with your mobile number and password resets by code. A text never contains a link. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/set-up-text-messages/') }}">Set up text messages</a></li>
              <li>Ask for a code by text before important changes, such as giving someone a role, so a stolen password alone can’t take over a website. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/confirm-important-changes/') }}">Confirm important changes</a></li>
            </ul>
          </section>
          <section class="feature-group" aria-labelledby="f-insight">
            <h3 id="f-insight">{{ m.icon('search') }} Search, analytics and the AI assistant</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
              <li>Site search on every page, with no outside service. It ignores capitals and accents, and marks matches in bold and underlined, not only in colour. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/search-your-website/') }}">Search your website</a></li>
              <li>Private analytics on your own server, with no cookies and no IP addresses stored. Every chart has a summary in words and the same data in a table. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/see-who-visits-your-website/') }}">See who visits your website</a></li>
              <li>An optional AI assistant, off for new sites, using your own key. It drafts and suggests; a person always decides, and AI-written alt text and translations must be checked before publishing. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/use-the-ai-assistant/') }}">Use the AI assistant</a></li>
              <li>A title, description and structured data for every page, a sitemap, and a Markdown version of each public page for AI tools. Each site decides how AI crawlers may use its content.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
          <section class="feature-group" aria-labelledby="f-design">
            <h3 id="f-design">{{ m.icon('theme') }} Themes and design</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
              <li>Choose a theme for each site and preview it first. Themes are installed on the server, never uploaded through the website. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/install-and-change-a-theme/') }}">Install and change a theme</a></li>
              <li>Change a theme’s colours for light and dark mode. A colour that would be too hard to read is refused, and the message names the colours that clash.</li>
              <li>Home, standard, landing, sidebar and full-width page layouts, each becoming a single column on a narrow screen. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/choose-a-page-layout/') }}">Choose a page layout</a></li>
              <li>Developers can start their own theme from the theme template, with checks and a tutorial. <a href="{{ docs('tutorials/create-a-theme/') }}">Create a theme</a></li>
            </ul>
          </section>
          <section class="feature-group" aria-labelledby="f-media">
            <h3 id="f-media">{{ m.icon('video') }} Media</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
              <li>Captions for videos in each of your site’s languages, and transcripts for videos and recordings. A page with a video or recording can’t be published without them. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/add-captions-and-transcripts/') }}">Add captions and transcripts</a></li>
              <li>Large files upload in parts, with progress announced to screen readers. Pause, resume or cancel, and carry on for up to a day if the connection drops. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/upload-large-files/') }}">Upload large files</a></li>
              <li>Upload limits for each site, and imports of very large files from the server. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/import-files/') }}">Import files from a folder</a></li>
              <li>Optional cloud storage, such as AWS S3 or Cloudflare R2, with a content delivery network; unpublished and members-only files stay protected. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/keep-files-in-the-cloud/') }}">Keep files in the cloud</a></li>
            </ul>
          </section>
          <section class="feature-group" aria-labelledby="f-running">
            <h3 id="f-running">{{ m.icon('settings') }} Running SightPress</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
              <li>Runs with Docker, on MariaDB, MySQL, PostgreSQL or SQLite, with FrankenPHP, nginx or Apache. <a href="{{ docs('getting-started/') }}">Getting started</a></li>
              <li>Turn optional features on or off for each site; turning one off keeps its data. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/turn-features-on-or-off/') }}">Turn features on or off</a></li>
              <li>Add features with modules from other developers, turned on only for the websites that need them. A broken or removed module never takes a website down. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/add-a-module/') }}">Add a module</a></li>
              <li>Developers can start their own module from the module template, with checks and a tutorial. <a href="{{ docs('tutorials/create-a-module/') }}">Create a module</a></li>
              <li>A command line tool for tasks such as creating a website. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/try-the-command-line-tool/') }}">Try the command line tool</a></li>
              <li>Update to a newer version, keeping every website. <a href="{{ docs('how-to/update-sightpress/') }}">Update SightPress</a></li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
        <p>Every change is listed in the <a href="{{ site.release.notes }}">{{ site.release.version }} release notes</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-alt" id="in-progress" aria-labelledby="progress-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">In progress</p>
        <h2 id="progress-title">Being built now: {{ site.next.version }}</h2>
        <p class="lede">The next release starts the work of getting SightPress ready for live websites.</p>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>A security review of the code, and checks that personal data never appears in error messages or logs.</li>
          <li>Tools to download your personal data or delete your account, and to choose how long data is kept.</li>
          <li>Faster pages, with page caching and performance budgets.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Plans for a release that isn’t out yet can still change.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="before-1-0" aria-labelledby="before-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">Planned</p>
        <h2 id="before-title">Before 1.0</h2>
        <p class="lede">Version 1.0 is the first version for live websites. Before it, we make SightPress safe, private, fast and fully documented.</p>
        <div class="split">
          <ul class="plain-list">
            <li><strong>Security:</strong> a full security review of the code, and checks that personal data never appears in error messages or logs.</li>
            <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> tools to meet UK and EU data protection law, so people can download their data or delete their account, and site owners can choose how long data is kept, with a generated privacy policy and cookie list.</li>
            <li><strong>Speed:</strong> page caching and performance budgets.</li>
          </ul>
          <ul class="plain-list">
            <li><strong>Running it for real:</strong> guides for running SightPress on a public server, on one server or several, and an upgrade tool.</li>
            <li><strong>Documentation:</strong> a guide or reference for every feature, command and setting.</li>
            <li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> an independent review, including blind and low-vision users, and a published accessibility conformance report.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-alt" id="after-1-0" aria-labelledby="after-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">Planned</p>
        <h2 id="after-title">After 1.0</h2>
        <p class="lede">After 1.0, SightPress grows with the people who use it. These are plans, and they may change.</p>
        <div class="split">
          <div>
            <h3>More help with accessible content</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
              <li>A link checker that finds broken links and links to documents that don’t say their type and size.</li>
              <li>Checks on uploaded PDFs, and a readability score for each language.</li>
              <li>Display preferences for visitors (text size, spacing, contrast and motion), without an overlay.</li>
              <li>An accessible form builder and an accessible audio and video player.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Moving from WordPress</h3>
            <p>The first module after 1.0 imports a WordPress site into SightPress.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Official modules</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
              <li><strong>For every site:</strong> news with feeds, events, a documents library, newsletters, and maps with text directions first.</li>
              <li><strong>For charities:</strong> donations with Gift Aid, volunteers and membership plans.</li>
              <li><strong>For public bodies:</strong> meetings and minutes, consultations, transparency data and emergency alerts.</li>
              <li><strong>For small businesses:</strong> catalogues, bookings and job vacancies.</li>
              <li><strong>For individuals:</strong> podcasts with transcripts, portfolios and CVs.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Further ahead</h3>
            <p>In time, SightPress could go beyond websites: events, bookings, courses and an online shop, then tools to run a small organisation, such as contacts, help desk and invoicing. Each would meet the same accessibility standard as the CMS.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="try" aria-labelledby="try-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="try-title">Try it, and tell us what you need</h2>
        <p class="lede">If you are a developer or a tester, you can run test release {{ site.release.version }} on your own computer today. If SightPress is missing something you need, we want to know.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="{{ docs('getting-started/') }}">{{ m.icon('settings') }} Try a test release</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=What%20I%20need%20from%20SightPress">{{ m.icon('mail') }} Tell us what you need</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="{{ site.github }}">Follow on GitHub {{ m.icon('external-link') }}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
{% endblock %}
